==Yoruba==

===Alternative forms===
*{{alter|yo|pụpa}} {{q|Ekiti}}

===Etymology===
Compare with {{cog|ife|kpikpa}}, probably from a {{m|yo|reduplication of '''{{l|yo|pa|t=to be red}}'''}}, which follows the general pattern of the other basic color roots, which involve a duplication of monosyllabic verbs. See {{l|yo|dúdú|t=[[black]]}}, a reduplication of {{l|yo|dú|t=to be dark}} and {{l|yo|funfun}}, a reduplication of {{l|yo|fun|t=to be white}}. Proposed to be derived from {{inh|yo|alv-yrd-pro|*-kpa}}

Perhaps related to {{cog|fon|kpákpá|t=a tree with red wood}}, proposed by Westerman to be derived from {{inh|yo|nic-vco-pro|*pia}}

===Pronunciation===
*{{yo-IPA|pupa}}

===Noun===
{{yo-noun|pupa}}
# [[red]]; that which is [[red]]

===Verb===
{{yo-verb|pupa}}
# to be [[red]]; to become [[red]]
#:{{syn|yo|pọ́n|rẹ̀ dòdò}}
# to be [[light]] in [[color]], usually in regard to [[skin]] [[tone]]

